# Beszel secrets. Two files, both mode 600, both gitignored via the root
# .gitignore's `.env.*` rule. Only this example is tracked.
#
# scripts/install.sh generates both on first run -- you should not need to
# write either by hand. It is documented here so the values are explicable.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- .env.beszel-hub
#
# USER_EMAIL / USER_PASSWORD create the dashboard account on FIRST BOOT only.
# After the SQLite database exists they are inert; changing them later does
# nothing. The password is generated by install.sh and is not something you
# ever type -- see AUTO_LOGIN.
USER_EMAIL=you@example.com
USER_PASSWORD=<generated by install.sh>

# The no-auth switch. Authenticates EVERY request as USER_EMAIL: no login
# screen, straight to the dashboard.
#
# The one you'll find in search results, DISABLE_PASSWORD_AUTH, is NOT this --
# it forces OAuth, which is the opposite of what you want.
#
# The consequence is the whole reason the hub binds 127.0.0.1: anything that
# reaches the port is logged in. Never bind this to 0.0.0.0 or a LAN address.
#
# It covers the regular user, not the PocketBase superuser. Admin screens
# (/_/ -- raw collections, backups) still prompt. USER_PASSWORD is that
# password, which is why install.sh keeps it rather than discarding it.
AUTO_LOGIN=you@example.com

# Used for links the hub generates. Must match how you actually reach it.
APP_URL=https://cachyos.tail4f0f0b.ts.net:8444

# -------------------------------------------------------------- .env.beszel-agent
#
# The hub's ed25519 PUBLIC key, generated on the hub's first boot and read out
# of ~/.local/share/beszel/hub/id_ed25519 by install.sh. The hub connects out
# to the agent over SSH and authenticates with the matching private key.
#
# Public keys are not secret. This file is 600 for consistency with the hub's,
# not because the value is sensitive.
KEY=ssh-ed25519 AAAA...
